From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:14:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LvglPkg: Use the per-flag setters of LVGL v9.6

LVGL v9.6 deprecates lv_obj_add_flag(), lv_obj_remove_flag() and
lv_obj_has_flag() for a setter and a getter of each flag
(lv_obj_set_hidden(), lv_obj_is_hidden() and the others), and v10
removes them. 0020 kept the 54 calls of lv_port_indev.c and of the
display engine with -Wno-deprecated-declarations.

Call the setters and the getters instead, one for one. In v9.6,
lv_obj_add_flag() and lv_obj_remove_flag() call those same setters,
which change nothing when the flag has the value already, and
lv_obj_has_flag() reads the same fields. LV_OBJ_FLAG_USER_1 has no
setter of its own: lv_obj_set_user_flag() and lv_obj_get_user_flag()
with bit 0 (LVGL_USER_FLAG_ROWS) set and read the same bit of
user_flags. Both INF files drop -Wno-deprecated-declarations, so that
a deprecated call stops the -Werror build again.

TEST=LvglPkg.dsc builds with GCC -Werror (RELEASE, X64) and no
warning; LvglSetupDxe.efi is the same, byte for byte.
